  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Concession",
     "texto": [
      "**Embora seja difícil, vamos avançar** (although it's difficult, we'll keep going). **Embora** and **ainda que** usually take the subjunctive. With a noun or infinitive **apesar de** is used: **Apesar da chuva, saímos** (despite the rain, we went out); **apesar de estar cansado, continuou** (despite being tired, he / she carried on)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Purpose",
     "texto": [
      "**Para que** + subjunctive usually has a different subject: **Expliquei devagar para que todos percebessem** (I explained slowly so that everyone would understand). With the same subject, **para + infinitive** is common: **Estudei para perceber melhor** (I studied to understand better)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Structure",
